n is a separate ingredient.","citation_ids":["circuit-r2-26-cite-external-mode-energy"],"evidence_ids":[],"id":"circuit.external_mode_energy","kind":"claim","label":"One persistent Gaussian mode and rooted energy induction","locator":"05-seed-simulation.tex:749–874; lem:seed-gram-induction, eq:seed-vacuum-weyl-gram, eq:seed-energy-weyl-sum","source_id":"circuit-r2-26-source-seed","statement":"The finite-word Gram induction adjoins formal orthogonal external modes ℓ,w to the endogenous rooted space. Echo parameter t=σ/2 realizes a requested seed angle σ through q(w), reusing the same mode at every seed gate and independent modes across vertices. The manuscript also evaluates ⟨h,Lh⟩ for finite spin–Weyl sums h and uses orthogonality of external and endogenous directions to pass the rooted energy, not only the vector Gram entries.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/circuit.external_mode_energy","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/circuit.external_mode_energy","id":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/edges/%5B%22circuit.external_mode_energy%22%2C%22circuit.gaussian_root_calculus%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/edges/%5B%22circuit.external_mode_energy%22%2C%22circuit.gaussian_root_calculus%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","semantic_class":"curated_argument_support","to":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/circuit.gaussian_root_calculus"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/circuit.external_mode_energy","id":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/edges/%5B%22circuit.external_mode_energy%22%2C%22circuit.singular_echo%